### Try these in VS Code (REST Client extension) or Rider / Visual Studio.
@host = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Public: list products (no token)
GET {{host}}/api/products

### 2. Create without token -> 401 Unauthorized
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Monitor", "price": 199.99, "stock": 10 }

### 3. Register a normal user
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "alice", "password": "secret123" }

### 4. Login as alice -> copy the token into @token below
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "alice", "password": "secret123" }

### 5. Create with token -> 201
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE
POST {{host}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Monitor", "description": "27 inch", "price": 199.99, "stock": 10 }

### 6. Update
PUT {{host}}/api/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Keyboard v2", "price": 69.99, "stock": 30 }

### 7. Delete as alice -> 403 Forbidden (needs Admin)
DELETE {{host}}/api/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Login as the seeded admin, then repeat #7 with the admin token -> 204
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "Admin123!" }
